		expectRed: ["packages/rph-application/src/handlers/recomposition-inarrow-set.test.ts"],
		why: "The site's JAN-CMDPRE DWP-03 comment states the promise: \"RecompositionContract.status has THREE in-arrows to EVALUATING — READY (first pass) and CONFLICTED/INSUFFICIENT ('re-evaluation after remediation'). No separate re-evaluation command exists … so BeginRecomposition IS the re-evaluation driver.\" Who relies on it: any professional whose recomposition landed INSUFFICIENT — an unacceptable required child or a failed whole-check — and who then remediates. Because no other command drives this machine to EVALUATING, dropping INSUFFICIENT from the source set does not merely refuse one call, it withdraws the re-evaluation capability entirely for that outcome, stranding the contract in INSUFFICIENT forever with the parent's completion permanently unreachable. The triage's own proposed mutation dropped CONFLICTED and INSUFFICIENT together and WAS killed — but only by the CONFLICTED test, so it would have credited a guard over a three-member promise on the evidence of two. The assertion now derives the member set from the contract's own binding table (BINDINGS: BeginRecomposition -> EVALUATING, from 'READY | CONFLICTED | INSUFFICIENT') instead of retyping it, drives each member through engine.dispatch, and names the offending member in the failure. A fourth in-arrow added to the contract later joins the sweep automatically, and one that cannot be reached fails loudly rather than being skipped.\n\nOBSERVED: BEFORE WRITING: the recorded mutant `fromStates('READY', 'CONFLICTED')` — dropping only INSUFFICIENT — left dwp03-precondition-coverage.test.ts at 16 passed (16) and every BeginRecomposition drive site in the repo green: dwp03 + recomposition + pwu-recomposition + disclosure-observed = 4 files / 65 passed (65). It SURVIVED. AFTER WRITING recomposition-inarrow-set.test.ts: clean 3 passed (3); under the same mutant 1 failed | 2 passed (3), failing 'EVERY declared source state is accepted — no member of the set is left unguarded' with \"BeginRecomposition REFUSED a source state the contract declares … Offending member(s): INSUFFICIENT (REJECTED: RPH_ILLEGAL_STATE_TRANSITION)\". CONTROL PROVEN SEPARATELY: its own mutant `fromStates('READY','CONFLICTED','INSUFFICIENT','EVALUATING')` reddens ONLY the control ('a re-issue from EVALUATING is the true NOOP and must be refused': expected 'ACCEPTED' to be 'REJECTED'), leaving the sweep green — 1 failed | 2 passed. SET SHOWN NON-VACUOUS: under the triage's own proposed mutant (`fromStates('READY')`) the sweep names BOTH other members — \"Offending member(s): CONFLICTED …, INSUFFICIENT …\" — so all three derived members are genuinely driven. Production file restored byte-identical after every run.",
		source: "JAN-PFA S3.3 increment 3 (the remaining 87 bare exports); triage claimed a precise assertion already existed and the RUN adjudicated that claim"
