		why: "PROMISE (JAN-ESCREC D3; the ER-1 app re-verifier's finding [2]; the .designerhead markup comment): while a candidate is staged the composition advisory hangs out of flow below the header box, whole and readable. WHO RELIES: the professional reading the advisory about the staged candidate's graph; with none staged, the advisory hanging from the lifecycle row below the bar. WHAT THE MUTATION DOES: makes the header box clip its overflow; the advisory, positioned against that box and lying wholly below it, is cut away entirely (and below the bar when nothing is staged), while its items' boxes, and the banner's last phrase inside the box, are unchanged. The third fix round holds each visible advisory item, in resume-hint.e2e.ts, inside the padding box of every ancestor whose overflow is not visible. Driven on the third fix round's final tree: KILLED by its victim (1 red). OBSERVED: KILLED — 1 test(s) red in resume-hint.e2e.ts: 'e2e\\\\resume-hint.e2e.ts:25:2 › Assurance floor — the resume hint names the recorded cause › an unregistered clean draft is described as an INCOMPLETE review, not' (Error: an ancestor clips the composition advisory); 1 failed",
