		why: "PROMISE (JAN-ESCREC D3; the ER-1 app re-verifier's findings [4] and [6]; describeRefusedEvidence's docblock): beside a work product whose floor passed, the refusal names each refused command result and why, and a result whose floor recorded no observation says so, before the engine's text. WHO RELIES: the operator reading why a step that passed its own floor did not complete. WHAT THE MUTATION DOES: the satisfied arm prints only the refused results that carry an observation; beside an INCONCLUSIVE result that observed nothing it says 'the command evidence did not pass its own floor:' and then names no result and no reason before the engine's text, the empty colon REG-F-415 named and the shape MAJOR 1 named. The third fix round adds that satisfied-arm case to begin-execute-escalated-review.test.ts — the command result's reviewer skipped the last criterion and recommended SATISFIED — whose evidence half must contain '(npm test): no observation recorded (floor.reasoning-review=INCONCLUSIVE). CompleteExecutionStep: '. Driven on the third fix round's final tree: KILLED by its victim (1 red). OBSERVED: KILLED — 1 test(s) red in begin-execute-escalated-review.test.ts: '⭐ JAN-ESCREC D3 — the execution plane says what an escalated review asks, on both arms > ⭑ the work product PASSED and a command result’s review observed NOTHING: the refusal says so, naming INCONCLUS' (AssertionError: the refusal does not name the command: expected ' CompleteExecutionStep: CompleteExecu…' to match /^evd_\\w+ \\(npm test\\): /) ⭐ RE-OBSERVED 2026-10-08 (`JAN-PRQUAL` `PQ-1`): still KILLED; the refusal now prints the command's argv as one line of JSON (design D2), where the text above quotes it as (npm test): KILLED — 1 test(s) red in begin-execute-escalated-review.test.ts: '⭑ the work product PASSED and a command result’s review observed NOTHING: the refusal says so, naming INCONCLUSIVE, before the engine’s text' (AssertionError: the refusal does not name the command: expected ' CompleteExecutionStep: CompleteExecu…' to match /^evd_\\w+ \\(\\[\"npm\",\"test\"\\]\\): /)",
