		why: "PROMISE (JAN-ESCREC D3; the ER-1 app re-verifier's finding [1], decided: after the hint chain, BEFORE the waiver note and form): the informational line sits beside the hint it qualifies. WHO RELIES: the professional reading the floor panel top to bottom, for whom the recommendation is part of why publishing is blocked, not a footnote to recording accepted risk. WHAT THE MUTATION DOES: renders both sentences after the waiver note and the 'Record accepted risk' form; the hint stays on screen and the line still follows it. The third fix round asks the line to precede the waiver's form beside the REJECTED and the INCOMPLETE review, and the waiver's note once one is recorded (assurance-floor-escalated-review-hint.e2e.ts's expectTheLineInItsPlace). Re-pointed in the fourth fix round (er1/f4): the hint and the line now render first in the panel's body and the waiver's note and form after the findings and the reviewer's answer, so the find spans from the line's block to the form's end and the replace moves the line's block after the form; the form is offered only beside a review carrying a finding, so its limb is the REJECTED case's. Driven on the fourth fix round's final tree (er1/f4): KILLED by its victim (1 red). OBSERVED: KILLED — 1 test(s) red in assurance-floor-escalated-review-hint.e2e.ts: 'e2e\\\\assurance-floor-escalated-review-hint.e2e.ts:345:2 › Assurance floor — an escalated review is routed to a human › ⭐ a review REJECTED for a finding, its rev' (Error: the escalation line is rendered after the waiver form); 1 failed; 2 passed (18.7s)",
