		expectRed: ["apps/rph-demo/e2e/assurance-floor-escalated-review-hint.e2e.ts"],
		why: "PROMISE (JAN-ESCREC D3; the second fix round's re-verifier's finding [2]; decided: the line follows the hint and precedes the waiver's affordances): the informational line comes before the note a recorded waiver adds, as before the form that records one. WHO RELIES: the professional reading a waived floor top to bottom, for whom the recommendation is part of why publishing is blocked, not a footnote to the waiver. WHAT THE MUTATION DOES: renders the waiver's non-discharge note between the hint and the line; the line still follows the hint and precedes the form, so only a page with a waiver recorded can tell. Re-pointed in the fourth fix round (er1/f4): the hint and the line now render first in the panel's body and the waiver's note after the findings and the reviewer's answer, so the find spans from the line's block to the note's end and the replace moves the line's block after the note, before the form. Driven on the fourth fix round's final tree (er1/f4): KILLED by its victim (1 red). OBSERVED: KILLED — 1 test(s) red in assurance-floor-escalated-review-hint.e2e.ts: 'e2e\\\\assurance-floor-escalated-review-hint.e2e.ts:345:2 › Assurance floor — an escalated review is routed to a human › ⭐ a review REJECTED for a finding, its rev' (Error: the escalation line is rendered after the note a recorded waiver adds); 1 failed; 2 passed (20.5s)",
